      },
      "provenance:relationshipType": "consulted",
      "provenance:contribution": "Queue V2 uses short immediate write transactions and WAL-backed snapshot\nisolation based on SQLite's transaction and isolation documentation\n([SQLite, n.d.-a](./REFERENCES.md#sqlite-isolation);\n[SQLite, n.d.-b](./REFERENCES.md#sqlite-transaction)). Electron's\n`utilityProcess` lifecycle and message-port contract informed the supervised\nworker boundary\n([Electron, n.d.-e](./REFERENCES.md#electronjs-org-docs-latest-api-utility-process)).\nSQLite remains the only durable queue store. Utility workers never settle task\nrows.",
      "provenance:target": [
        {
          "@id": "target:area%3Ainfluence%2Frepository-engineering"
        }
      ],
      "provenance:confidence": "unknown",
      "prov:generatedAtTime": "2026-09-24"
    },
