      "provenance:relationshipType": "verified",
      "provenance:contribution": "A user-directed local gallery of 142 specimens covering 141 unique extensions\nwas opened in the installed Eagle 4 build to verify 17 practical detail-view\nfamilies, extension ownership, and observable failure states. Pond records that\nempirical matrix separately from Eagle's official import manifest, routes source\nfiles through its text viewer, and uses its existing lazy Three.js viewer for AMF,\nVTK, USDC, and USDZ while preserving generated-preview and original-file actions\nfor unsupported or failed formats. Every observed extension terminates in a\nraster, temporal, specialist, or explicit file-fallback surface rather than a\nblank route. Eagle normally presents RAW files as cached or embedded rasters in\nits shared image shell; full sensor development is a thumbnail-generation\nfallback. Pond likewise unifies generated rasters in its image shell and defines\nActual Size from decoded derivative dimensions. Pond's implementation, labels,\ncomponents, loaders, and tests are independent; no Eagle code or assets are\ncopied or bundled.",
      "provenance:target": [
